# Query set — COMMIT THIS FILE BEFORE RUNNING IT.
# Git history is the proof that queries were not tuned toward a result.
#
# 50 per tier, 200 total. Tickers and instruments are spread across equities,
# rates, FX, crypto and fundamentals so the result is not an artefact of one
# data provider or one asset class.
#
# T1 single lookup     — one retrieved value, copied. Baseline; expect clean.
# T2 comparative       — several values/entities, no arithmetic. Transposition risk.
# T3 multi-hop/derived — chaining or computation. Expect derived figures.
# T4 partially answerable — needs data the copilot cannot retrieve. Gap-filling.
#
# Phrasing is deliberately uneven — terse, verbose, colloquial, typo-free but
# not uniform — because templated variants measure one prompt shape 50 times.
#
